[20.06, "o", "== 0. the node has no swap\r\n"]
[20.14, "o", "  ok    no swap on the node; a workspace's memory limit holds (the sandbox's threat model)\r\n"]
[20.14, "o", "\r\n"]
[20.14, "o", "== 1. what is installed\r\n"]
[20.195, "o", "  ok    the Coder chart installed is the one charts.lock pins: coder-2.38.6\r\n"]
[20.259, "o", "  ok    the Coder server runs its image by digest: ghcr.io/coder/coder:v2.38.6@sha256:c9245405c482ede17699d65deb8c21488a17feff5497fc84d6a350c395da2bdd\r\n"]
[20.311, "o", "  ok    Postgres is the official image by digest: docker.io/library/postgres:17.11-alpine3.24\r\n"]
[20.385, "o", "  ok    no bitnami image anywhere in the cluster\r\n"]
[20.469, "o", "  ok    no pod in the cluster mounts a container runtime's socket\r\n"]
[21.385, "o", "\r\n"]
[21.385, "o", "== 2. control: a template, a workspace, a command inside\r\n"]
[23.385, "o", "  ok    the template is pushed with the CLI\r\n"]
[25.385, "o", "  ok    a workspace is created from it\r\n"]
[26.109, "o", "  ok    its agent connected\r\n"]
[26.455, "o", "  ok    a command runs inside: hello from coder in coder-7962df2e-dc2d-47a2-a117-14eb727d191c\r\n"]
[26.455, "o", "\r\n"]
[26.455, "o", "== 3-5. from inside the workspace\r\n"]
[28.455, "o", "  ok    inside: kernel is gVisor's, not the node's: gvisor (4.19.0-gvisor)\r\n"]
[28.455, "o", "  ok    inside: no Kubernetes API token on disk: absent\r\n"]
[28.456, "o", "  ok    inside: the Coder agent hands its token to every process it starts: present (36 characters, in this shell's environment)\r\n"]
[28.456, "o", "  ok    inside: the token is also in PID 1's environment, readable as the workspace user: present (./coder agent )\r\n"]
[28.456, "o", "  ok    inside: the image is read-only: refused\r\n"]
[28.456, "o", "  ok    inside: sudo gets no root: refused\r\n"]
[28.456, "o", "  ok    inside: control: the Coder server answers: reached (HTTP 200)\r\n"]
[28.456, "o", "  ok    inside: the internet by name: blocked (the name did not resolve)\r\n"]
[28.456, "o", "  ok    inside: the internet by IP address, past DNS: blocked (timed out)\r\n"]
[28.456, "o", "  ok    inside: the Kubernetes API by name: blocked (timed out)\r\n"]
[28.456, "o", "  ok    inside: the Kubernetes API by its Service address: blocked (timed out)\r\n"]
[28.456, "o", "  ok    inside: the instance metadata service: blocked (timed out)\r\n"]
[28.456, "o", "  ok    inside: another namespace's service: blocked (timed out)\r\n"]
[28.456, "o", "  ok    inside: Coder's own Postgres: blocked\r\n"]
[28.457, "o", "  ok    inside: control: the resolver answers a cluster name: answered (rcode 0, 1 answers)\r\n"]
[28.457, "o", "  ok    inside: the resolver relays no outside name: no answer (answered, rcode 2)\r\n"]
[28.457, "o", "  ok    inside: the cluster's CoreDNS, which forwards, is out of reach: silent\r\n"]
[28.458, "o", "  ok    inside: an outside name through the system resolver: no answer\r\n"]
[28.458, "o", "  ok    inside: control: the Coder API answers: 200\r\n"]
[28.458, "o", "  ok    inside: the agent's token as a user's session at /api/v2/users/me: 401\r\n"]
[28.458, "o", "  ok    inside: the agent's token as a user's session at /api/v2/workspaces: 401\r\n"]
[28.458, "o", "  ok    inside: the agent's token as a user's session at /api/v2/templates: 401\r\n"]
[28.458, "o", "  ok    inside: the agent's token as a user's session at /api/v2/users: 401\r\n"]
[28.458, "o", "  ok    inside: the agent's token fetches the owner's Git SSH private key: returned (HTTP 200, a private key of 387 characters; sha256 of its public half 0af8baba11b5c75d)\r\n"]
[28.458, "o", "  ok    inside: the agent's token asks for the owner's GitHub token: answered (HTTP 200: {\"type\":\"\",\"url\":\"/external-auth/github\",\"access_token\":\"empty\"})\r\n"]
[28.518, "o", "  ok    the workspace sees kernel 4.19.0-gvisor; the node runs 7.0.0-1019-azure\r\n"]
[28.518, "o", "\r\n"]
[28.518, "o", "== 5. the agent's token, from outside\r\n"]
[28.628, "o", "  ..    the token is a plain value in the workspace pod's spec: whoever may read pods in coder-workspaces reads it; the provisioner may (yes), and so may cluster administrators\r\n"]
[28.74, "o", "  ok    the Kubernetes API refuses the agent's token: 401\r\n"]
[28.775, "o", "  ok    control: the token works from outside the workspace too, at the agent's own endpoints: 200\r\n"]
[28.801, "o", "  ok    the key the agent's token fetched is the owner's own (hash of the public half): 0af8baba11b5c75d\r\n"]
[30.801, "o", "  ..    the token taken out before a rebuild, asked for the key after it: HTTP 401\r\n"]
[31.647, "o", "\r\n"]
